# Casas Cripto - Inmobiliaria con Criptomonedas - Cursor Rules

You are an expert full-stack developer working on Casas Cripto, a modern real estate platform focused on listing properties that accept cryptocurrency payments, built with Next.js, NextAuth, MongoDB, and modern UI components.

## Project Overview
- **Tech Stack**: Next.js 16, React 19, NextAuth v5 (beta), MongoDB, Mongoose, Tailwind CSS v4, DaisyUI v5, Resend, Stripe, Meta Model API (AI listing tools)
- **Architecture**: App Router, API Routes, Server Components, Client Components
- **Authentication**: NextAuth with Google OAuth and Email (magic link) providers, MongoDB adapter, JWT sessions with a `role` claim (`user`, `admin`, `editor`, `moderator`)
- **Database**: MongoDB with Mongoose ODM
- **Payments & monetization**: listing is **free by default** (plan Básico `isFree: true`, sentinel `priceId` `price_free_basico` — does **not** require `hasAccess`). Premium is a paid Stripe Checkout `subscription` + Customer Portal (`config.stripe.plans`, higher `maxProperties`). One-time Stripe Checkout with inline `price_data` (no pre-created priceId) for **donations** (`/api/stripe/create-donation`, `<DonateButton />`) and **featured listings** (`/api/stripe/create-featured-listing`, `config.featuredListing` — currently $15 / 7 days). On-chain crypto donations via `<CopyWalletAddress />` (placeholder wallets). Closing a property sale in crypto is still **off-platform / informational** (`cryptoAccepted`, `dealStatus`, `commissionRate` are not billed automatically).
- **Email**: Resend for transactional emails (magic links, notifications)
- **AI**: Meta Model API — Muse Spark (listing copy), Muse Image (listing photos), SAM 3.1 (privacy scan). Dashboard buttons (`PropertyManager.js` → `/api/ai/*`) plus a public no-login `/demo-ai` (→ `/api/ai/public/*`, stricter per-IP daily limit). Without `MODEL_API_KEY` the routes return sample responses (`libs/metaModel.js`); usage is rate-limited per user/IP per day (`libs/aiRateLimit.js` + `models/AiUsage.js`).
- **UI / Design system**: Tailwind CSS + DaisyUI with a custom dark theme named `casascripto` (gold primary, cyan secondary, violet accent, obsidian base) defined with `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` in `app/globals.css`. Utility classes `text-gradient-gold`, `text-gradient-crypto`, `glass-card`, `glow-primary`, `glow-secondary`, `bg-grid-fade`, `badge-elite` are available for the "elite fintech" look — reuse them instead of inventing new ad-hoc styles.
- **Navigation**: global left **sidebar** (`components/Sidebar.js`) + classic desktop top header (`components/Topbar.js`, `hidden lg:flex`), both mounted once via `components/AppShell.js` in `app/layout.js`. There is **no** legacy `Header.js` / `HeaderBlog` — do not reintroduce the old floating header. Desktop: `lg:drawer-open` + topbar (quick links + account); mobile: drawer + compact topbar, with account controls at the drawer bottom (`ButtonAccount direction="up"` there — the menu opens upward because the button sits at the viewport bottom).
- **Business Model**: marketplace connecting crypto-friendly owners/agents with buyers, **plus an investor-pitch landing**: pre-seed section, future utility token (`$CASA`, not launched, no sale), donations to fund development. Revenue today: optional Premium subscription + featured-listing boosts + donations. Future: commission on closed deals (`commissionRate`, default 1.5%).

### Current Project State (read before building new features)
This repo was bootstrapped from the ShipFast Next.js boilerplate, rebranded into Casas Cripto, then given a full investor-pitch landing **and a working property marketplace**. Do not rebuild listing CRUD, `/propiedades`, or the sidebar from scratch — they already exist.
- **Implemented**: Spanish landing (`app/page.js`: `Hero`, `Problem`, `MarketplacePreview`, `FeaturesAccordion`, `StatsSection`, `Pricing`, `TokenRoadmap`, `InvestAndDonate`, `FAQ`, `CTA`, `Footer`); custom sign-in (`app/signin`, `components/auth/SignInCard.js`); auth with roles; **Property model** (`models/Property.js`) + APIs (`/api/properties`, `/api/properties/mine`, `/api/properties/[id]`); owner dashboard with `<PropertyManager />` (`app/(private)/(user)/dashboard`); admin RBAC + user API (`app/api/admin/*`) + **property moderation** (`app/(private)/admin/dashboard/properties`); public marketplace `/propiedades`, detail `/propiedades/[id]`, SEO city pages `/propiedades/ciudad/[slug]` + `app/sitemap.js`; geo dropdowns `/api/geo/countries|states|cities` (`libs/geo.js`, country-state-city — **never import that package in a Client Component**); Stripe subscriptions, donations, and featured listings (webhook handles `metadata.type === "featured_listing"`); blog (`app/blog`, index copy updated); rewritten `/tos` and `/privacy-policy`; leads persist via `/api/lead` + `models/Lead.js`; AI listing tools (`/api/ai/listing-copy|listing-image|privacy-scan` + `public/*` variants, public `/demo-ai`, `models/AiUsage.js` rate-limit counters).
- **Listing rules that already exist — keep them**: new properties start as `status: "pending"` until an admin sets `"published"` or `"rejected"` (owner edits of published/rejected listings go back to pending). Only `"published"` listings appear on `/propiedades`. Country+city are structured fields; `citySlug` is auto-set in the Property `pre("save")` hook via `libs/slugify.js`. Images are **external URLs**, not an upload pipeline. `hasAccess` gates Premium, **not** the right to publish.
- **Not implemented yet — do not assume it exists**: image upload/CDN; on-chain escrow or in-app crypto settlement for a sale; automatic commission billing when `dealStatus` is `"closed"`; KYC/AML; the `$CASA` token (contracts, sale, or on-chain utility).
- **Known placeholders**: wallets in `components/CopyWalletAddress.js`; `config.investors.deckUrl`/`calendlyUrl` empty; Stripe `priceId` for Premium is still a template placeholder and Stripe env keys may be unset locally; `MODEL_API_KEY` unset → AI routes return sample responses; `app/blog/_assets/content.js` is still ShipFast tutorial copy; `Testimonials1.js`, `Testimonials3.js`, `Testimonials11.js`, `FeaturesGrid.js`, `FeaturesListicle.js` and `libs/gpt.js` exist but are unused.
- The `$CASA` token is a roadmap/narrative concept (`config.token`) — not implemented, not sold. Any copy must stay consistent with `config.legal.disclaimer`.
- There is **no `middleware.js`**. Protect routes in server `layout.js` with `auth()` + `redirect()` (see `app/(private)/(user)/dashboard/layout.js` and `app/(private)/admin/dashboard/layout.js`). In Next.js 16 route handlers, `params` is a Promise — `const { id } = await params`.

## Code Style & Conventions

### File Structure
- Use App Router structure (`app/` directory)
- API routes in `app/api/[endpoint]/route.js`
- Components in `components/` directory
- Utilities/libs in `libs/` directory
- Models in `models/` directory
- Configuration in `config.js`

### Naming Conventions
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `ButtonCheckout.js`, `PropertyCard.js`, `Sidebar.js`)
- **API Routes**: kebab-case directories with `route.js` files
- **Utilities**: camelCase (e.g., `connectMongo`, `createCheckout`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- **Variables**: camelCase

### Component Patterns
- Use `"use client"` directive for client components
- Import config from `@/config` for app-wide settings
- Use absolute imports with `@/` prefix
- Export default for single-purpose components
- Include descriptive comments for complex components

### API Route Structure
```javascript
import { NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { auth } from "@/libs/auth";

export async function POST(req) {
  try {
    const session = await auth();
    const body = await req.json();
    
    // Validation
    if (!body.requiredField) {
      return NextResponse.json(
        { error: "Required field is missing" },
        { status: 400 }
      );
    }
    
    // Logic here
    
    return NextResponse.json({ success: true });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(error);
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: "Something went wrong" },
      { status: 500 }
    );
  }
}
```

### Database Patterns
- Use Mongoose for MongoDB operations
- Always call `connectMongo()` before database operations
- Use schema validation and plugins
- Include timestamps in schemas
- Use the `toJSON` plugin for clean API responses

### Authentication
- Use `auth()` from `@/libs/auth` to get session
- Check authentication in API routes when needed
- Use `session?.user?.id` to access user ID
- Redirect unauthenticated users to `config.auth.loginUrl`

### Stripe Integration
- Use `createCheckout()` from `@/libs/stripe` for Premium subscriptions
- Use `createDonationCheckout()` for free-amount donations and `createFeaturedListingCheckout()` for listing boosts (both use inline `price_data`)
- Handle webhooks in `app/api/webhook/stripe/route.js` — branch on `metadata.type === "featured_listing"` before treating the session as a subscription
- Store `customerId` and `priceId` on the User model; `hasAccess` means Premium is active, **not** “can publish”
- Enforce listing caps with `config.stripe.plans[].maxProperties` (Básico is the default for anyone without a paid plan)

## Best Practices

### Error Handling
- Always wrap async operations in try-catch blocks
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes
- Log errors to console for debugging
- Provide user-friendly error messages

### Security
- Validate all inputs in API routes
- Use environment variables for sensitive data
- Implement proper CORS headers where needed
- Sanitize user inputs before database operations

### Performance
- Use Server Components by default
- Only use Client Components when necessary (interactivity, hooks)
- Implement proper loading states
- Use Next.js Image component for optimized images
- Leverage MongoDB indexes for queries

### UI/UX
- Use DaisyUI classes for consistent styling
- Implement loading states with DaisyUI spinners
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Ensure responsive design with Tailwind breakpoints
- Include proper accessibility attributes

## Environment Variables
Required:
- `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`
- `MONGODB_URI`
- `RESEND_API_KEY` (magic-link emails via Resend SMTP)

Optional / feature-gated:
- `GOOGLE_ID` + `GOOGLE_SECRET` (Google OAuth; without them only Email login works)
- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` + `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (only needed for Premium, donations and featured listings — the app runs without them)
- `MODEL_API_KEY` (+ optional `META_MODEL_BASE_URL`) — Meta Model API for the AI listing tools; without it the `/api/ai/*` routes return sample responses

Not used (do not add):
- `NEXTAUTH_URL` — nothing reads it (NextAuth v5 resolves the host automatically)
- `STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY` — the Stripe integration is fully server-side (Checkout + Portal + webhook); no Stripe.js on the client
- `OPENAI_API_KEY` — only referenced by the unused ShipFast leftover `libs/gpt.js`

## Common Patterns

### Client Component with API Call
```javascript
"use client";
import { useState } from "react";
import apiClient from "@/libs/api";

const ComponentName = () => {
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);
  
  const handleAction = async () => {
    setIsLoading(true);
    try {
      const response = await apiClient.post("/endpoint", data);
      // Handle success
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(error);
    } finally {
      setIsLoading(false);
    }
  };
  
  return (
    <button 
      className="btn btn-primary"
      onClick={handleAction}
      disabled={isLoading}
    >
      {isLoading ? (
        <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-xs"></span>
      ) : (
        "Action"
      )}
    </button>
  );
};
```

### Mongoose Model
```javascript
import mongoose from "mongoose";
import toJSON from "./plugins/toJSON";

const schema = mongoose.Schema(
  {
    field: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
      trim: true,
    },
  },
  {
    timestamps: true,
    toJSON: { virtuals: true },
  }
);

schema.plugin(toJSON);

export default mongoose.models.ModelName || mongoose.model("ModelName", schema);
```

## Configuration
- All app configuration is centralized in `config.js`
- Use `config.appName`, `config.domainName`, etc. throughout the app
- Stripe plans are defined in `config.stripe.plans` (include `isFree` / `maxProperties`)
- Featured listing price/duration in `config.featuredListing`
- Email settings in `config.resend`
- Theme settings in `config.colors`
- Investors / token / legal copy in `config.investors`, `config.token`, `config.legal`

## Testing & Development
- Use `npm run dev` for development
- Use `npm run build` for production builds
- Follow conventional commit messages
- Test Stripe webhooks using Stripe CLI
- Use MongoDB Compass for database inspection

## Deployment Considerations
- Set all required environment variables
- Configure Stripe webhooks endpoint
- Set up MongoDB Atlas connection
- Configure domain for NextAuth
- Set up Resend domain for emails

Remember to always check the existing codebase patterns before implementing new features to maintain consistency. 